the function at cs:29e build code on the stack. than it calls cs:5e66 which calls this code
the stack is [b8 01 02 bb 62 7c b9 14 {w:arg1 - 4600} {w:default_drive} 90 90 cb]

arg1 in practice is always 23 therfore
23 - 4600 = 23 + ba00 = ba23
default_drive will usually be 1 for A

so the code will end up something like 

0x0000000000000000:  B8 01 02       mov  ax, 0x201
0x0000000000000003:  BB 62 7C       mov  bx, 0x7c62
0x0000000000000006:  B9 14 23       mov  cx, 0x2314
0x0000000000000009:  BA 01 00       mov  dx, 1
0x000000000000000c:  90             nop  
0x000000000000000d:  90             nop  
0x000000000000000e:  CB             retf 

however none of these registers is actually used directly after the call
the code is cleaned from the stack